# Environment variables for the Alta Mortgage Group site.
#
# The site deploys to VERCEL. Set these in the Vercel project:
#   Vercel → altamortgage-website3 → Settings → Environment Variables
# For local development, copy this file to .env.local.
#
# Variables marked (Vercel-managed) are injected automatically when you
# create the resource from the Vercel Storage tab. Do not set them by hand.

# Public site URL (used by metadata, sitemap, robots, and resume links)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://altamortgagegroup.net

# Google Analytics / Tag Manager (optional)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=GTM-XXXXXXX

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — Neon Postgres  (STRONGLY RECOMMENDED)
#
# Persists leads, applications, and in-progress drafts, and records the
# delivery status of each. Without it, the MISMO document in Blob storage is
# the only copy of an application and nothing can be looked up by reference
# number; drafts stay in the applicant's browser only.
#
# Create: Vercel → Storage → Create Database → Neon → connect to this project.
# Then run db/schema.sql once in the Neon SQL Editor.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=            (Vercel-managed — pooled connection string)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MISMO document storage — Vercel Blob  (REQUIRED for /apply)
#
# Every submitted application is written as a MISMO v3.4 (ULAD/URLA) XML file
# before anything else happens. Blobs are written with private access; there
# is no public URL for a mortgage application.
#
# Create: Vercel → Storage → Create Database → Blob → connect to this project.
#
# Without the token the app falls back to local disk, which on Vercel is
# read-only and discarded after each request — every submission would record
# mismo_status = failed. Local development uses ../storage/mismo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=   (Vercel-managed)
# MISMO_STORAGE_DIR=       (local dev only; defaults to ../storage/mismo)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email  (RECOMMENDED)
#
# Sends the loan officer a summary of each application with the MISMO document
# attached.
#
# The APPLICANT also receives email from the website (never from the CRM):
#   - on submit, a confirmation with the document checklist and where to send it
#   - if they stop partway, up to three reminders with a resume link (see the
#     Resumable drafts section below)
# The website does not email applicants for anything else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SMTP_HOST=smtp.your-host.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=notifications@altamortgagegroup.net
SMTP_PASS=your-smtp-password
NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=loans@altamortgagegroup.net

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRM integration  (OPTIONAL, best effort)
#
# Leads and applications are forwarded to the Alta CRM's /api/website-lead
# endpoint, which creates the lead, logs an activity note, notifies the owner
# and texts the admins.
#
# This forward is best effort: three attempts, then given up on. It is NOT a
# system of record — Blob storage and the database above are. Leaving these
# unset degrades to "no CRM"; it does not stop applications from being stored.
#
# CRM_API_KEY must MATCH the WEBSITE_API_KEY environment variable on the CRM.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CRM_API_URL=https://altamortgagecrm.net/api/website-lead
CRM_API_KEY=your-shared-secret-matching-WEBSITE_API_KEY-on-the-crm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resumable drafts + abandonment reminders  (OPTIONAL)
#
# Once an applicant completes step 1 (name + email), the wizard saves their
# progress server-side so they can finish on another device. If they stop,
# they get up to three reminder emails (1 hour, 24 hours, 7 days after their
# last edit), each with a resume link and a stop link. Unfinished drafts are
# deleted after 30 days. Drafts never contain the SSN.
#
# Requires the database above. Without CRON_SECRET and DRAFT_LINK_KEY, drafts
# still save and the applicant's own browser can still resume; only the
# emailed reminders are disabled.
#
# Generate each value separately with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#
# DRAFT_LINK_KEY encrypts the resume token at rest so a database dump alone
# cannot be turned into working links. Keep a copy somewhere that is not
# Vercel. If it changes, reminders for existing drafts stop (they cannot be
# decrypted); new drafts are unaffected.
#
# Scheduling: Vercel Cron on the Hobby plan runs once a day at most, so the
# 15-minute trigger is a GitHub Actions workflow instead —
# .github/workflows/draft-reminders.yml. It needs, in the GitHub repo:
#   Secret   CRON_SECRET   (same value as below)
#   Variable SITE_URL      (this deployment's URL)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRON_SECRET=
# DRAFT_LINK_KEY=
